1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:05,544
Suppose your team keeps asking Copilot to
organize the same evidence before

2
00:00:05,544 --> 00:00:06,931
requesting a review.

3
00:00:07,111 --> 00:00:12,317
Each time, the agent needs the issue, a
summary of the diff, and the test result.

4
00:00:12,497 --> 00:00:17,189
A skill is a package the agent can use
when that kind of task comes up.

5
00:00:17,369 --> 00:00:22,015
We will start with three steps and one
result that a human can inspect before

6
00:00:22,015 --> 00:00:23,523
sending it to a teammate.

7
00:00:24,965 --> 00:00:30,180
In the training repository, create a
project skill named prepare p r evidence.

8
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:35,830
Under the dot GitHub skills folder, give
it a directory with the same name and add

9
00:00:35,830 --> 00:00:37,698
a file called skill dot M D.

10
00:00:37,878 --> 00:00:40,366
The header contains a name and
description.

11
00:00:40,546 --> 00:00:45,268
State which request it is for, so both the
teammate invoking it and the client

12
00:00:45,268 --> 00:00:47,266
selecting it have a clear signal.

13
00:00:48,715 --> 00:00:53,807
In the body, ask for the issue, the
changed behavior, and the result of a real

14
00:00:53,807 --> 00:00:54,395
test run.

15
00:00:54,575 --> 00:00:56,912
Define how to handle missing inputs.

16
00:00:57,092 --> 00:01:01,562
If the test output is absent, call that
out so the author can supply it.

17
00:01:01,742 --> 00:01:04,454
Keep this first skill as a short
procedure.

18
00:01:04,634 --> 00:01:09,337
The human author reviews the resulting
draft and decides what to publish.

19
00:01:09,517 --> 00:01:13,241
Tool permissions and repository controls
still apply.

20
00:01:14,715 --> 00:01:17,510
Open a fresh Copilot chat in the project.

21
00:01:17,690 --> 00:01:22,551
Verify discovery in the customizations
view, then invoke the skill through the

22
00:01:22,551 --> 00:01:25,480
slash menu when the approved setup
supports it.

23
00:01:25,660 --> 00:01:29,746
Give it the synthetic issue, the diff, and
the passing test output.

24
00:01:29,926 --> 00:01:33,627
Read the draft and map each claim back to
a supplied source.

25
00:01:33,807 --> 00:01:38,814
Check that the procedure gives a teammate
a more consistent result than rewriting

26
00:01:38,814 --> 00:01:40,174
the request each time.

27
00:01:41,632 --> 00:01:46,080
Repeat the invocation in a new chat, this
time without the test output.

28
00:01:46,260 --> 00:01:49,642
Expect the draft to say that verification
is missing.

29
00:01:49,822 --> 00:01:54,182
If it reports a green run from the issue
description alone, tighten the

30
00:01:54,182 --> 00:01:56,146
instructions and rerun the case.

31
00:01:56,326 --> 00:02:01,563
Now ask an unrelated question, such as
explaining a Python expression, and check

32
00:02:01,563 --> 00:02:03,526
whether the skill is relevant.

33
00:02:03,706 --> 00:02:07,419
This gives you a small repeatable test of
behavior and scope.

34
00:02:08,882 --> 00:02:12,914
Place this skill beside the instruction
file from the previous lesson.

35
00:02:13,094 --> 00:02:16,294
The instruction file carries project
conventions.

36
00:02:16,474 --> 00:02:19,144
The skill carries the reusable procedure.

37
00:02:19,324 --> 00:02:22,460
Tools perform actions such as reading a
file.

38
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:28,594
An approved M C P connection can expose
additional tools or resources in another

39
00:02:28,594 --> 00:02:29,488
environment.

40
00:02:29,668 --> 00:02:32,753
This skill works using supplied files and
outputs.

41
00:02:32,933 --> 00:02:38,404
Access remains governed by the selected
client, its tools, and the organization's

42
00:02:38,404 --> 00:02:39,012
settings.

43
00:02:40,465 --> 00:02:45,359
Pick a second recurring task, such as
summarizing a failed training test for the

44
00:02:45,359 --> 00:02:45,788
author.

45
00:02:45,968 --> 00:02:50,554
Write a name, a description, a short
procedure, and the expected output.

46
00:02:50,734 --> 00:02:54,158
Try it with complete input and with one
item missing.

47
00:02:54,338 --> 00:02:58,882
Ask a teammate to judge both responses
using the same criteria.

48
00:02:59,062 --> 00:03:03,780
Share the versioned file once you can
explain when it applies and show that it

49
00:03:03,780 --> 00:03:05,837
handles the missing input clearly.
